BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (  In the beginning, the gods created a sacred river that flowed between two villages. Each dawn,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (     the river delivered five silver coins to the village of the Senders. The Givers faced a cho) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (    ice: keep their coins or cast them into the waters.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (  The river held ancient magic-any coin surrendered would multiply threefold by the time it reac) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (    hed the village of the Receivers downstream. There, the Receivers could keep their bounty or) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (     send portions back upstream, where the current carried it unchanged.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (  At first, fear ruled both villages. Senders clutched their coins, and the river ran dry. Famin) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (    e came to both settlements.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (  Then a wise woman named Galen proposed a covenant: "Trust begets trust. Send forth generously,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (     and return fairly what you receive. The river multiplies our gifts, but only cooperation mu) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (    ltiplies our fortune.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (  The villages began to send and return with open hearts. Prosperity flowed in both directions. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (    Some rounds were generous, some modest, but the balance held. They learned that the river's ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (    magic worked only when both villages honored the cycle.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (  The gods smiled, for they had taught mortals that abundance comes not from hoarding, but from ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (    the sacred circle of giving and receiving.) Tj ET
