BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (  **The Parable of the Echo Springs**) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (  In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite sides of a valley, separated by the Echo Spri) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (    ngs-pools of water that mysteriously tripled whatever was placed within them.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (  The villages were suspicious of one another. One year, during a terrible drought, a young vill) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (    ager named Kira received her family's last five measures of grain. Desperate, she walked to ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (    the springs and called across to the other village: "I entrust this to you!" She threw three) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (     measures into the spring.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (  The waters churned, and nine measures appeared on the far shore. The villagers there were amaz) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (    ed. They could have kept everything, but their elder remembered the old ways. "Trust begets ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (    trust," she said. They returned six measures through the springs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (  Back at Kira's village, eighteen measures emerged-more than enough for both communities. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (  From that day, the villages prospered by taking turns giving and returning through the springs) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (    , each act of faith multiplied threefold, each gesture of reciprocity building greater abund) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (    ance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (  The springs still flow today, teaching us that wealth grows not when hoarded, but when shared ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (    wisely between those who trust and honor one another. The greatest prosperity comes to those) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (     who give generously and return faithfully.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (Reasoning:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (  The user is asking me to write a 200-word myth that reflects how the trust game should be play) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (    ed. Since this is the beginning of the experiment and I haven't played any rounds yet, I sho) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (    uld write a myth that reflects good principles for playing the game.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (  The trust game is fundamentally about:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (  1. Trust - the sender must trust the receiver to return some amount) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (  2. Cooperation - both parties benefit when they cooperate) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (  3. Reciprocity - the receiver should reciprocate the sender's trust) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (  4. Mutual benefit - the multiplication factor means both can gain if they work together) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (  I should write a myth that embodies these principles. Let me create a story that illustrates t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (    he value of trust, reciprocity, and cooperation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (  I'll use classic mythic elements - perhaps about sharing, trust, and mutual benefit. Let me ai) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (    m for exactly 200 words.) Tj ET
