BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (      In the beginning, the gods created a sacred river that flowed between two villages. Each d) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (        awn, the river delivered five silver coins to the village of the Senders. The Givers fac) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (        ed a choice: keep their coins or cast them into the waters.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (      The river held ancient magic-any coin surrendered would multiply threefold by the time it ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (        reached the village of the Receivers downstream. There, the Receivers could keep their b) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (        ounty or send portions back upstream, where the current carried it unchanged.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (      At first, fear ruled both villages. Senders clutched their coins, and the river ran dry. F) Tj ET
