BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (      # The Myth of the Two Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (      In the beginning, two rivers flowed through separate valleys-the River of Dawn and the Riv) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (        er of Dusk. Each carried only enough water to sustain its own people through harsh seaso) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (        ns.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (      The River of Dawn received a blessing: each season, the heavens gifted it five vessels of ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (        sacred water. But the water only nourished what it touched directly. The people of Dawn ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (        lived, but barely.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (      One season, an elder suggested: "Let us send our water to the River of Dusk. Though it see) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (        ms foolish, the ancient texts speak of multiplication through trust.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (      Reluctantly, they sent three vessels downstream. As the water flowed into Dusk's valley, a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (         miracle occurred-it multiplied threefold, becoming nine vessels. The people of Dusk rej) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (        oiced, their crops flourishing beyond memory.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (      Dusk's council debated: "Should we return something to Dawn, who trusted us?") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
