BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (      In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite sides of a valley, separated by the Echo ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (        Springs-pools of water that mysteriously tripled whatever was placed within them.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (      The villages were suspicious of one another. One year, during a terrible drought, a young ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (        villager named Kira received her family's last five measures of grain. Desperate, she wa) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (        lked to the springs and called across to the other village: "I entrust this to you!" She) Tj ET
