BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (      # The Tale of the Twin Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (      In the beginning, the goddess Aethera created two villages separated by a barren valley. E) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (        ach village had a sacred spring that produced five measures of water daily-enough to sur) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (        vive, but never to flourish.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (      One day, a drought threatened both villages. A wise elder from the First Village proposed:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (         "Let us send our water across the valley. Perhaps the gods will bless the gift.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (      When the water crossed the valley floor, it flowed through enchanted soil that tripled its) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (         volume. The Second Village received fifteen measures! Overjoyed, they held council: "We) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (         have received abundance. Let us return generously to those who trusted us.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (      They sent back ten measures, which also tripled in the crossing. The First Village now had) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (         thirty measures from their initial sacrifice of five!) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (      Word spread to Aethera, who smiled upon the valley. "You have learned the secret of the en) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (        chanted soil," she proclaimed. "Trust is the seed. Reciprocity is the harvest.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (      From that day forward, the villages prospered, each taking turns sending water first, alwa) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (        ys returning more than required. The barren valley transformed into fertile ground where) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (         both communities thrived, sustained not by hoarding their springs, but by sharing them.) Tj ET
